Z||000001||Joe Torma||10-07-2001||04:01 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>Anyone have any good suggestions for brands/models?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My brother(works at body shop) and father(garage painter) use SATA guns.  Little expensive, but professional qualitly/results.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||10-07-2001||08:30 PM||||We have 3 different conventional suction feed DeVillbiss guns, and we bought about a year ago a DeVillbiss Millenium GTi gravity feed HVLP gun, very nice!<P>It ran us about $350 for the HVLP gun, not sure about the other ones, we've had them for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||10-07-2001||11:41 PM||||I have a SATA nr92 that I picked up at a pawn shop for $50 and a Accuspray Issac HVLP that I bought new.  I love them both.  Mostly I use the SATA for primer and the Accuspray for base/clear.  But I have sprayed base/clears with the SATA.||||reg||1
Z||000004||k2m4||10-09-2001||12:10 PM||||Devillbis gun in my opinion are the best BUT when i started to paint the guy who tought me would always say its not how expensive the gun is its the painter behind the gun. Ive seen him paint in a dank corner of a garage and have paint jobs come out like glass. just my .02 cents<P>kerm<BR>86 2M4<BR>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||EdsB52||10-09-2001||12:18 PM||||If you want a smokin price on a quality gun, try these guys:<P>"http://www.allsprayguns.com/"<P>I've bought from them and am very happy.||||reg||1
